{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>בתוכחות</b> — in the manner of 'and reprove with affliction' — we know that You discipline a man on account of his iniquity with afflictions." "<b>חמודו</b> — the desire of his body. And behold, his desire was vanity."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra paraphrases the phrase as an allusion to Job's words; the second clause appears to be his explanatory gloss on the concept of reproof-through-suffering."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:19.856981285Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}